# BIMI Mark Verifying Authority roots.
#
# A Verified Mark Certificate is only worth anything if it chains to an authority that actually verifies who
# owns a mark, so these are pinned here rather than taken from the chain a sender supplies or from the
# device's TLS trust store, which answers an entirely different question.
#
# Source: the Mark Verifying Authorities listed at https://bimigroup.org/vmc-issuers/, plus GoDaddy, whose
# mark CP/CPS is at https://github.com/godaddy/cp-cps/blob/main/cpcps/MarkCPCPS.md.
#
# Only self-signed roots are included; intermediates arrive with the certificate being checked.
# Fingerprints are asserted in MvaRootsTest, so replacing a root fails the build rather than silently
# trusting a different authority.
#
# Corroboration beyond the list itself:
#   DigiCert - identical to https://cacerts.digicert.com/DigiCertVerifiedMarkRootCA.crt and to the root in
#              the chain published by paypal.com.
#   Entrust  - verified to have signed the intermediate in a live chain published by a retailer using an
#              Entrust-issued mark certificate.
#
# DigiCert
